WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.650
It might seem as though in order to be named
the highest paid movie actor of the last decade,

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.420
one would have had to star in a good number
of huge Hollywood hits.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:13.200
But with only a handful of roles over the
last ten years, it comes as something of a

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.610
surprise that Will Smith has been crowned
the king of Hollywood paychecks.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:22.510
The actor didn't totally dominate pop culture
in the 2010s like he had in the 1990s with

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:27.720
The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air and the Bad Boys
franchise, or in the 2000s with high-profile

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:34.380
appearances in everything from romantic comedies
to post-apocalyptic actioners to Oscar-nominated dramas.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.860
Instead, the 2010s saw Smith taking quite
a few dramatic roles, in films like Focus,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:43.210
Concussion, Collateral Beauty, and Gemini
Man.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.760
He also turned out appearances in two critical
failures: as Floyd Lawton, a.k.a. Deadshot,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:54.560
in the much-maligned Suicide Squad, and as
Daryl Ward in Bright, another David Ayer-directed venture.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.120
Smith's final film role of the 2010s was different
from all the aforementioned others: he voiced

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:05.650
Lance Sterling, "the world's most awesome
spy," in the 20th Century Fox animated flick

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.100
Spies in Disguise opposite Spider-Man star
Tom Holland.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.930
Though Smith hasn't exactly had a stellar
critical record for this decade of film releases,

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.450
there has been one shining star: Men in Black
3.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.150
It's been a long while now, but Men in Black
3 was released in this decade, in 2012, to

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:26.800
be exact, and it earned Smith an incredible
$100 million paycheck.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.360
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Smith
walked away with that stack of cash from the

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.220
film's box office take-home.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:39.640
In 2019 cash, $100 million is nearly $112
million, further solidifying Smith as the

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.820
top-earner of the decade.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:47.689
For Men in Black 3, Smith reprised his role
as Agent J one last time for an up-front salary

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:53.170
of $20 million, but secured in his contract
a whopping 10 percent of gross income from

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:56.360
the film, which is where the extra $80 million
came from.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:02.100
Usually, after-release supplementary compensation
for an actor is calculated by net profit once

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.240
studio bills and marketing expenses are paid,
so a deal like Smith's is extraordinary.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.740
Franchise star power is what keeps sequels
alive, and many studios have grown eager to

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:18.000
shell out money to retain actors, or, in Smith's
case, bring them back an entire decade after

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.220
the previous iteration.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:24.190
The Men in Black 3 production rolled out the
metaphorical red carpet for Smith all throughout

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.610
shooting as well, and was even ignobly memorialized
in New York Post spreads complaining about

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:33.300
the luxurious trailer Smith brought along
for on-location shoots.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.660
"Where'd you get the car?"

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:35.340
"And the suit?"

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.920
"I stole them both.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.460
Car from your wife, suit from your grandmother."

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.940
Bringing back the namesake Men in Black was
an extremely expensive venture, but in the

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:51.319
end it paid off: Men in Black 3 grossed the
most money of the franchise's history, including

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:55.540
the most recent and poorly-performing foray,
Men in Black: International.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:03:00.420
It's unlikely Smith will ever return to the
MIB franchise, and truthfully, after a payday

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.430
like the one he received for Men in Black
3, he doesn't really need to.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:09.750
Knowing that Smith's 2010s haul came from
a blockbuster franchise isn't surprising.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.650
What is surprising is that the franchise was
anything other than the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:20.980
Iron Man's 2008 release dawned our new blockbuster
movie-going era, and the 2010s saw it become

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.260
a franchise-perpetuating machine.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.900
Profits had never been greater for the tentpole
release than they were in the 2010s, and that's

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.960
been nothing but good for film studios and
the actors who negotiate themselves into long-term contracts.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:37.680
It's the kind of money that will not only
set them for life, but also pay their great-grandchildren's

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:38.959
college tuitions.

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:42.950
Robert Downey Jr. has been without a doubt
Marvel's reigning star.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.760
But still, the Iron Man lead couldn't take
the title of the top-earning actor of the

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:53.519
2010s, even with $75 million for Avengers:
Infinity War and Avengers: Endgame each.

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:58.349
RDJ actually did come in second place for
single-film income, behind Smith.

